<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khoja Niyaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1889–1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Khoja Niyaz Hajji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khoja Niyaz was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> leader from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hami">Kumul</a> (Hami) who headed the Kumul rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> provincial government from 1931. In 1933 he was named president of the First East Turkestan Republic at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>, although he never governed from there. He later came to terms with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheng-shicai">Sheng Shicai</a> and served in the provincial government, but was arrested and executed in 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khoja-niyaz.jpg" alt="Khoja Niyaz" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hoja-Niyaz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
